    Milestone 12 phase 0: the contracts, and phase 1: release hygiene
    
    Contracts before code, as every milestone since 7 has done.
    
    docs/threat-model.md is what the milestone's security review is run
    against: eight trust boundaries with what crosses each and what is
    left over, the attacker models the review works through, and the nine
    invariants a finding would falsify. SECURITY.md keeps its scope list
    and points at the reasoning behind it.
    
    docs/soak.md fixes the soak suite before it exists — the workload, the
    four injected faults, the nine invariants asserted after every round,
    and what it does not cover. Decision 0013 replaces the calendar-shaped
    exit criterion ("a full support window", 90 days) with a stated budget,
    and records that the database fault is container loss and recovery, not
    a promoted replica. Decision 0012 decides what 1.0 freezes: Public
    becomes semver-covered, held by a committed signature baseline rather
    than by care; the console names, the dashboard, the triggers, the
    snapshot, the tracer, and both bundled connectors are promoted;
    ExecutionStore stays Experimental, which is 0006 holding.
    
    The post-1.0 policy that docs/releases.md had deferred to this milestone
    is written: the versioning rules, the removal path, and the long-term
    support window — the last minor of an outgoing major gets security
    fixes for 12 months after the next major. SECURITY.md carries the same
    window. compatibility.md records why the deprecation marker stays a
    docblock rather than PHP 8.4's attribute: the floor is 8.2, and the
    attribute emits the runtime notice this project declines to emit.
    
    The roadmap records both amendments with their reasoning, including
    that the security review is internal and says so — running one and
    calling it external would be the first dishonest line in the repo.
    
    Phase 1, the hygiene a 1.0 cannot carry: the pre-0.6.0 make:* generator
    forwarders are removed, 1.0 being the last release allowed to remove
    them, and the test that held them now holds something more durable —
    every command Laraflow registers is named under the laraflow: prefix.
    CONTRIBUTING states that release tags are annotated and, once a key is
    configured, signed. The empty unreferenced .env.example is gone with
    the .gitignore entry that preserved it and the export-ignore line for
    it; the .gitattributes comment now names MAINTAINERS.md, which has
    shipped in the dist archive since 0.7.0 without being listed.
    
    Pint, PHPStan level 8, and 1438 tests green; the docs site builds with
    no dead link.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

