    silently skipped, so earlier work was undone while it stood — the
    exact thing the stop rule exists to prevent, and its guard was
    unreachable. A definition fault routed past compensation, making the
    undo depend on *how* the workflow broke. A resumed pass rebuilt its
    failure as a WorkflowException, overwriting error_class. The
    cancellation cascade and the attention scan could not see a
    compensating execution. joinPolicy() was published and never read; it
    is now matched on exhaustively, so a second case is a compile-time
    obligation rather than silence.
    
