    [debug-db] Milestone 6 step 5c: count matched rows, not changed bytes
    
    The duplicate-delivery failure gave the diagnosis away: recordDispatch
    treats zero affected rows as 'execution not found', and the test
    dispatches the same execution three times inside one frozen second, so
    the second write is byte-identical — and MySQL and MariaDB count rows
    changed, not rows matched. Same disease at the checkpoint (a step that
    leaves the context alone reads as a lost claim), release, cancellation,
    and the retention scrub, whose dry run must agree with the real run.
    
    This is a production defect on the most-deployed Laravel engine, not a
    test arrangement problem: a worker checkpointing an unchanged context
    in the same second as its previous write would throw ClaimLostException
    and roll back real work.
    
    The fix makes the two counts the same thing everywhere: the executions
    table gains a version column and every repository write bumps it
    through counted(), so an update that matched cannot report zero. Not
    optimistic locking — nothing reads the number — just a guaranteed
    change per write. Schema edited in place under the pre-freeze policy.
    
