    Milestone 6 step 4a: support Laravel 13, and make the PHP floor real
    
    The first CI run on this repository failed in both PHP 8.2 cells, and
    the message named the wrong culprit: laravel/pint ^1.32 requires PHP
    ^8.3, so a package declaring php ^8.2 could not install its own dev
    dependencies there. A formatter's floor is not the package's floor.
    Pint relaxes to ^1.30 — Composer resolves 1.30.4 on 8.2 and 1.32.1 on
    8.3+, and the lint job runs on 8.4 either way. Reproduced locally with
    config.platform.php before changing anything, which is the only reason
    the real cause was visible at all.
    
    Assessing that properly turned up the larger gap: Laravel 13 has been
    out since February and this package declared ^12.0 only, so it does
    not install on the current major. It does now — illuminate/* widen to
    ^12.0|^13.0, Testbench to ^10.12|^11.0 — and the suite is green on
    both majors, which took two real fixes rather than a constraint edit.
    Laravel 13 makes ConnectionInterface::transaction() generic, so the
    repository's transaction() helper declares the callback return type it
    was always passing through; and Laravel 13 brings Guzzle 8, where
    ResponseException requires the response argument Guzzle 7 defaulted.
    Both fixes hold on Laravel 12.
    
    PHP 8.5 joins the matrix, which is now 8 cells: 8.2–8.5 against both
    majors, minus 8.2+Laravel 13, which Laravel itself does not allow.
    
    Laravel 11 and below stay unsupported, and compatibility.md now says
    why instead of only saying so. Laravel 10 and 11 are past their
    bug-fix windows; Laravel 10 wants only PHP 8.1, which reached security
    end-of-life in December 2025, and these value objects are final
    readonly classes — 8.2 syntax. Widening to a major upstream no longer
