    for a dropped connection or a momentary 503, with millisecond backoff
    and deterministic jitter. It is the inner loop to the step policy's
    durable outer one, and three rules keep the two from multiplying: it
    ships with max_attempts = 1; it never waits in-process for a Retry-After
    longer than max_retry_after but returns the response, so the step can
    fail and retry durably on the provider's own schedule; and a request
    that is not idempotent is repeated only on 429, which was never
    processed, or when the caller marked it safe with asIdempotent().
    
