    Step and execution events now carry how long the work took, so a
    listener can build latency metrics without re-reading the database or
    subtracting timestamps itself.
    
    WorkflowStepCompleted and WorkflowStepFailed carry the attempt's own
    duration. The StepAttempt record that goes to history is hoisted into a
    variable and feeds both the write and the event, so telemetry and the
    stored history cannot disagree about how long a step took — they are
    one value, not two computations of it.
    
