    name could not be used. "Terminal" already means *never claimable
    again* in the lifecycle contract — completed and cancelled — while
    `failed` is explicitly re-executable. The question durations and the
    coming retention work actually ask is "has this stopped?", which
    includes failed. The method is therefore isFinished(), matching the
    finished_at column exactly, with both the enum and the changelog
    spelling out why the two concepts stay apart: conflating them would let
    a retention policy either skip failed work forever or delete work a
    worker still owns.
    
