    cancelled alike. Retention scans and "finished between" filters would
    otherwise need a three-way coalesce over completed_at, failed_at, and
    cancelled_at, which no index can serve. It is cleared by markRunning(),
    and by the claim's compare-and-set update: `failed` is re-executable,
    so without that a reclaimed execution would carry a stale finish and
    look eligible to retention while a worker was actively running it. The
    compare-and-set cancellation path, which writes the row directly rather
    than through the handle, makes the same write and is tested separately.
    A `retrying` execution deliberately records no finish — it is waiting,
    not finished, and retention deleting it would destroy a scheduled retry.
    
