    persisted and announced (WorkflowStepFailed) as it happens — timeouts
    included — the remaining steps run, and the execution then ends failed,
    recording and rethrowing the first step's exception, so 'a failed
    execution throws' holds for every caller. WorkflowExecutionFailed fires
    once, at the end. Re-executing skips completed steps and re-runs only
    the failed ones, exactly as under stop.
    
