    freely — even under a one-attempt policy, because worker death is not
    the step's fault — and the dead attempt is closed out in history as
    interrupted rather than erased. The same situation past the deadline is
    a timeout: the attempt is recorded as timed_out with a
    StepTimeoutException naming the missed deadline and charged to the
    retry policy exactly like a thrown failure — backoff if budget remains,
    terminal otherwise. Each new attempt gets a fresh deadline from its own
    start.
    
